# Published bundles are verified byte-for-byte by the loader before it runs
# them: it fetches the expected sha256 from the auth Worker and refuses to
# execute anything that does not match. That hash is computed at BUILD time
# over the exact UTF-8/LF bytes, so any line-ending normalisation between the
# build and what raw.githubusercontent serves would make every client fail to
# launch.
#
# Git must therefore never touch these files. They survive today only because
# git's content heuristic happens to classify them as binary; that is a
# property of the bytes, not a policy, and a future bundle could look textier.
# Declare it instead of relying on the guess.
#
# tools/publish_public.py refuses to publish into a checkout where these paths
# are not marked -text, and re-hashes each published file against its manifest.
games/**/bundle-obfuscated.lua -text
games/**/*.lua -text
load.lua -text
